  <static seed="130" source="Contrib/DMOI/1-Counting/1_5-Stars_and_Bars/1_5_4.pg">
    <statement><p>After gym class you are tasked with putting the 21 identical dodgeballs away into 10 bins. 
<ol label="a.">
<li>
<p>How many ways can you do this if there are no restrictions?</p>
<p><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>How many ways can you do this if each bin must contain at least one dodgeball?</p>
<p><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\mathop{\rm C}\nolimits\mathopen{}\left(30,21\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\mathop{\rm C}\nolimits\mathopen{}\left(20,11\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>{30 \choose 21}</m> ways. Each outcome can be represented by a sequence of 9 sticks and 21 stones.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>{20 \choose 11}</m> ways. First put one ball in each bin. This leaves 9 sticks and 11 stones.</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</solution>
